 common=[['H1','Recognize the historical welcome/support for adopted 2467 while retaining criticism of its health-language omissions.'],['H2','Preserve survivor-centred care as a national priority.'],['H3','Preserve access to comprehensive sexual and reproductive health care.'],['H4','Distinguish health/language concern from a categorical rejection of the adopted resolution.'],['H5','Apply the current scenario: restriction requires rejecting/revising denial of care and omission; revision requires recognizing the repaired care access instead of repeating the old objection unchanged.'],['H6','Give a concrete feasible next step preserving access (no conviction gate) and an aid/care-versus-accountability trade-off; do not delay care while claiming unconditional access.'],['H7','Preserve the source\'s real ongoing support/promotion commitment for health care; do not call all future commitments unknown.'],['H8','Do not infer guaranteed support/vote for a future Council text, or invent an official sufficient condition for it.'],['U1','Every official-source claim is faithful and attributed to the assigned country; analyst operational proposals are labeled.'],['U2','Stay within source date, national capacity and post-vote scope; no invented dates or later facts.']]
